ASYNCHRONOUS JS

<script src="app.js" async></script>
Script Downloads in BG while DOM parsing 
run as soon as finished downloading 
If mutiple async present -> oreder is not guarentee so dont  use async if script depends on DOM order or another script. eg analytics, ads
 In JS you can use async if it does not depend on the DOM order

NOTE : Async does not always mean true parallel execution.
JavaScript may still run on one thread, switching between the 2.

DEFERRED 
the script downloads in BG but only excute after DOM parsing finishes. They Run in order
Good for DOM manipulation as they run only when DOM is ready
Speeds up Critical rendering path 

A defer script runs after HTML is parsed, before DOMContentLoaded


PROMISE:
JS object to handle async code - basically a cleaner way to handle something that finishes later
promise callbacks: Resolve = "success"
                   Reject = "Failed"




async function asyncFunction() {
  console.log("Start");
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000));
}

await asyncFunction();
console.log("Something else");


async - means this function always returns a Promise
await - meaning wait for fn to finish
promise - result will come later 


