SKELETON
A skeleton screen is a temporary layout shown before full content loads.
only improves percieved performance no actual decrease in loading time 

PROGRESIVE RENDERING
loading the most important parts first. eg. Load header and main content first.
Load comments, ads, or sidebars later.

improves perceived speed and usability.

MINIFICATION
Reduce size of large JS/CSS
rm whitespace, long var names etc -> so debugging near impossible -> use only for deployments not dev
Tree shaking = removing unused code from JS/CSS bundles.

Smaller file -> fewer critical bytes -> faster downloads ->  fast load






